     </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dCcchCYJ5no\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf: Rebranded to Devin Desktop</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        On June 2, 2026, Cognition rebranded Windsurf to Devin Desktop. Existing users received an over-the-air update. Windsurf was kept available through July 1, 2026. After July 1, 2026, Devin Local became the only local agent option.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>\n                        <span>2026-06-02</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"feedback feedback-positive\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"As of February 2026, Windsurf ranked #1 in LogRocket's AI Dev Tool Power Rankings\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-source\">— LogRocket (positive)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/news-insights/company-news/github-copilot-is-moving-to-usage-based-billing/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Usage-Based Billing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot moved from flat-rate/request-based billing to usage-based billing using GitHub AI Credits. All plans now charge based on actual token consumption depending on the model used. Also introduced MAI-Code-1-Flash model, Copilot Max plan, pooled organization credits, and budget controls.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>\n                        <span>2026-06-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"feedback feedback-negative\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Usage paying for AI is 1000x crazier 4.6 each dollar spent is 27 dollars in copilot AI Credits\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Hacker News (negative)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI: v0.45.0 Release</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Released v0.45.0 on June 3, 2026 with safer auto-updates, improved terminal and WSL handling, faster and more reliable core behavior, and new user actions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span>2026-06-03</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"feedback feedback-negative\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Gemini CLI stopping work from June 18, 2026\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Hacker News (negative)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#entry-20260626-1833\" target=\"_blank\">AI Assistant Security Challenge</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        After 2,000 people tried to hack an OpenClaw test instance with 6,000 attempts and $500 in token spend, nobody managed to leak the secret using Opus 4.6.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#entry-20260626-1833\">Simon Willison</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#entry-20260626-1758\" target=\"_blank\">AI Review Agent Disagreement Loop</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Hypothetical incident report: two AI review agents entered a disagreement loop over a malicious package, costing $41,255 in inference spend before Finance revoked API keys.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#entry-20260626-1758\">Simon Willison</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">supply-chain</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-security</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/#entry-20260626-1710\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI GPT-5.6 Series Announced</a>\